            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Orson Welles' Early Years</strong><br>\nOrson Welles was born in Kenosha, Wisconsin, in 1915. He was a gifted child with a talent for the arts and began his career in theatre and radio. By the age of 20, he had already made significant strides in New York City's theatre scene, showcasing his flair for drama and direction.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Fame</strong><br>\nWelles' innovative radio productions, including a famous adaptation of \"The War of the Worlds,\" catapulted him to fame. His broadcast caused widespread panic among listeners who believed the Martian invasion was real, demonstrating the power of media and Welles' skill in using it.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Transition to Film</strong><br>\nAfter his success in radio, Welles moved to Hollywood to work in the film industry. His first project, \"Citizen Kane,\" was groundbreaking. Welles co-wrote, directed, and starred in the film, which is often hailed as one of the greatest movies ever made.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
