            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Challenges in Later Career</strong><br>\nLater in his career, Welles struggled to find the same level of success. He worked on a variety of international projects and became known for his distinctive voice work, including narrations and commercial voice-overs, to finance his own film projects.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Orson Welles as an Actor</strong><br>\nWelles was not only a director but also an accomplished actor. He appeared in front of the camera for many of his own films and took on roles in other directors' projects, displaying a wide range of performances that showcased his versatility.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Orson Welles</strong><br>\nOrson Welles died in 1985, but his influence on the film industry endures. His creativity, willingness to take risks, and mastery of multiple entertainment mediums have left a lasting imprint on the arts. Welles is remembered as a visionary who changed the landscape of cinema.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
